<header class="ref-head"><span class="hero-ornament"></span><h1 class="research-title">4 August in history</h1><p class="ref-lede">6 events that happened on 4 August, from 1265 to 1964.</p></header>
<ol class="day-events"><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1265 CE <span class="tih-ago">761 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Simon de Montfort is killed at the Battle of Evesham</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">The future Edward I defeated and killed Simon de Montfort at Evesham, ending the barons' rebellion against Henry III. Montfort's parliaments with elected burgesses outlived him.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb tih-event-hero"><p class="tih-hero-kicker">&#10022; Anniversary of the day</p><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/war-of-the-spanish-succession" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/war-of-the-spanish-succession.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1704 CE <span class="tih-ago">322 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Anglo-Dutch forces capture Gibraltar</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">A fleet under Admiral Sir George Rooke took Gibraltar during the War of the Spanish Succession. Ceded to Britain in 1713, it remains a British territory despite repeated Spanish claims.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag tih-tag-profile" href="/empire/spanish-empire">Spanish Empire</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/war-of-the-spanish-succession">War of the Spanish Succession</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gibraltar">Gibraltar</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1789 CE <span class="tih-ago">237 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">France's National Assembly abolishes feudal privileges</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">In a night session, nobles and clergy renounced their seigneurial rights, tithes and exemptions one after another. The decrees swept away much of the legal framework of the Ancien Régime.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1914 CE <span class="tih-ago">112 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Britain declares war on Germany</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">When Germany ignored an ultimatum to respect Belgian neutrality, Britain declared war at 11 pm London time. The British Empire's entry turned a continental war into a global one.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag tih-tag-profile" href="/empire/british-empire">British Empire</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/london">London</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1944 CE <span class="tih-ago">82 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Anne Frank and her family are arrested in Amsterdam</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">German police raided the secret annexe at Prinsengracht 263, arresting the Frank family and four others. Anne died in Bergen-Belsen in early 1945; her diary became a classic of Holocaust testimony.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/amsterdam">Amsterdam</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1964 CE <span class="tih-ago">62 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">US destroyers report a second attack in the Gulf of Tonkin</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">US warships reported an attack by North Vietnamese boats that probably never happened. Within days Congress passed the Gulf of Tonkin Resolution, authorising Johnson to escalate the Vietnam War.</p></div></li></ol>
